# GreenChainz — Cursor Rules
# Applied automatically to all AI suggestions in this repo.

## Stack
- Express 5 + tRPC 11 backend (NOT Next.js, NOT REST)
- Vite + React 19 SPA frontend
- TypeScript strict mode throughout
- Drizzle ORM + PostgreSQL
- pnpm ONLY (never npm, never yarn)

## Azure Infrastructure (All Services)
- Hosting: Azure Container Apps
- Auth: Azure Entra ID Easy Auth sidecar (prod) / registerDevAuthShim() (local dev only)
- Secrets: Azure Key Vault
- Database: PostgreSQL on Azure
- Storage: Azure Blob Storage
- AI: Azure OpenAI
- Search: Azure AI Search
- Maps: Azure Maps
- Queue: Azure Storage Queue
- Real-time: Azure Web PubSub
- Monitoring: Sentry
- DO NOT suggest AWS, GCP, Firebase, Supabase, Vercel, Railway, or Render

## Auth Rules
- User identity comes from server-side Easy Auth headers ONLY (X-MS-CLIENT-PRINCIPAL-*)
- Never read userId/orgId/role from request body or query string
- MANAGED_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID != CLIENT_ID — never mix them
- OAUTH_SERVER_URL goes in .env, NOT .env.local
- registerDevAuthShim() is for local dev only, always behind NODE_ENV !== 'production'

## Drizzle Schema
- All column types must be explicitly imported from drizzle-orm/pg-core
- Missing imports = ReferenceError crash at container startup
- After schema changes: pnpm run db:generate && pnpm run db:migrate

## Dead Services
- Autodesk SDA API: shut down April 2026, server/autodesk-sda-service.ts is a stub
- Do not call searchEpds() or getEpdDetail() — they return empty/throw
- For EPD data use EC3 (Building Transparency) or EPD International
- EpdLookupModal.tsx was deleted — do not recreate it

## Docker
- docker compose up --build for normal rebuilds
- docker compose build --no-cache app for schema/import changes
- Build runs: vite build (client) + esbuild server/_core/index.ts (server)
- Both must pass or the image fails

## General
- Never suggest Replit SDK
- BLUF (Bottom Line Up Front) in all explanations
- Priority #1 feature: SupplierOnboarding.tsx
- Business goal: 50 suppliers + 200 architects by Q2 2026
